From: ipad-rea <ipad-rea@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: hci_bcm: add BCM43291A0 (iPad 2 "n88" module)

The iPad 2 (iPad2,1 / k93ap) Bluetooth is a BCM43291A0 ("Olympic Second
Module", per the iOS 9.3.5 BlueTool strings; ADT uart3/bluetooth
"bluetooth,n88", product-id 4767, vendor-id 0x05ac).  hci_bcm's DT match
table has no entry for it, so the serdev driver never binds and there is
no Bluetooth.

Add the compatible.  No device data: like the other 43xx entries the
43291 uses the defaults (no autobaud quirks).

The patchram file name is derived at runtime from the chip's LMP
subversion via bcm_uart_subver_table (btbcm.c), which has no BCM43291
row either.  That row needs the subversion the chip actually reports;
it is read from the first boot's dmesg ("BCM (x.y.z) build NNNN" with
hw_name == NULL) and added in a follow-up patch.  Until then hci_bcm
binds and runs the chip on its default firmware at up to 1.5 Mbaud.

drivers/net/wireless note for the Wi-Fi half of the same module: the
Wi-Fi side is a BCM4329 on SDIO (ADT sdio node, wifi-chipset "43291",
IPSW firmware dir wifi/4329c0, NVRAM sromrev=3), already in brcmfmac's
SDIO table (SDIO_DEVICE_ID_BROADCOM_4329 = 0x4329) — no patch needed
there, only the s5l8940x SDIO host driver.

---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
index 0000000000..1111111111 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -1597,6 +1597,7 @@ static struct bcm_device_data cyw55572_device_data = {
 static const struct of_device_id bcm_bluetooth_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm20702a1" },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4329-bt" },
+	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm43291a0-bt" },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4330-bt" },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4334-bt" },
 	{ .compatible = "brcm,bcm4345c5" },
-- 
2.43.0

